This directory contains a manual test / usage demo of the GPlotDesigner family
of classes, which lets you produce ROOT (cmp. http://root.cern.ch) plots in an 
intuitive way. The library will create input files for ROOT, which can then be 
further processed.

In order to try out the example, after calling the executable, have a llok at
the file result.C with a text editor -- it was created with GPlotDesigner and
associated classes. Then, if ROOT is in your path, execute

root -l ./result.C

The same run also writes result.gp (the gnuplot backend, graph plotters only)
and result.py (the matplotlib backend). The matplotlib script is a self-
contained, headless (Agg) Python program; it ends without a savefig, so append
one and run it, e.g.:

    ( cat result.py; echo "fig.savefig('result.png')" ) | python3

The matplotlib backend supports the graph plotters (GGraph2D/2ED/3D/4D) and the
histogram plotters (GHistogram1D/GHistogram2D). Function plotters
(GFunctionPlotter1D/2D) are NOT yet supported on the matplotlib (or gnuplot)
backend -- they would require translating the ROOT TFormula formula dialect into
a NumPy-evaluable expression, which is deferred; use the ROOT backend for those.